1
00:00:03,906 --> 00:00:05,913
Style Transfer is a workflow

2
00:00:05,913 --> 00:00:08,986
with fifty-three built-in artistic presets.

3
00:00:09,098 --> 00:00:12,511
Describe a subject, then choose a look from the menu,

4
00:00:12,511 --> 00:00:15,177
from oil painting to art nouveau.

5
00:00:15,379 --> 00:00:17,459
The workflow generates the image,

6
00:00:17,459 --> 00:00:20,679
analyses it, and can refine the result for quality.

7
00:00:21,032 --> 00:00:22,403
Change the preset,

8
00:00:22,403 --> 00:00:25,860
and the same subject takes on an entirely new style.

9
00:00:37,301 --> 00:00:40,825
Image Studio can work on one prompt or a whole batch.

10
00:00:40,911 --> 00:00:43,626
Enter one prompt per line, choose the image

11
00:00:43,626 --> 00:00:46,340
model and aspect ratio, and start the run.

12
00:00:46,714 --> 00:00:49,100
Results collect in a gallery as they arrive.

13
00:00:49,430 --> 00:00:51,901
Reference images and optional prompt enhancement

14
00:00:51,901 --> 00:00:54,137
offer additional ways to guide the series.

15
00:01:08,447 --> 00:01:12,564
Video Studio brings motion into the same creative process.

16
00:01:12,637 --> 00:01:15,006
Standard mode supports individual shots,

17
00:01:15,006 --> 00:01:18,844
while Batch mode accepts a list of prompts or a folder of images.

18
00:01:18,978 --> 00:01:21,734
Choose the model, duration, and aspect ratio,

19
00:01:21,734 --> 00:01:24,023
then follow the generation progress.

20
00:01:24,222 --> 00:01:26,030
Story and thematic tools provide

21
00:01:26,030 --> 00:01:28,216
another route for connected sequences.

22
00:01:42,875 --> 00:01:46,849
Workflows chain several creative steps into one recipe.

23
00:01:46,958 --> 00:01:49,130
This one generates a draft image,

24
00:01:49,130 --> 00:01:52,856
analyses it to extract a rich description, then regenerates

25
00:01:52,856 --> 00:01:55,833
from that enriched prompt for higher quality.

26
00:01:55,986 --> 00:01:57,810
Fill in a prompt, an aspect ratio,

27
00:01:57,810 --> 00:01:59,543
and what to avoid, then run it.

28
00:01:59,610 --> 00:02:01,864
When it finishes, both the draft

29
00:02:01,864 --> 00:02:04,776
and the final image are ready to compare.
